    "title": "Reflection:",
    "placeholder": "Enter your reflection here.",
    "long_instructions": "## Final Project \r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/18c2321f0c5f2626200d4c872239ac1c-image-1771608745433.png\" alt=\"Sample student project of a website for ordering food from a burrito bowl websit\"  width=\"300px\" style=\"border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0 20px 10px 10px;\">\r\n\r\n#### At the beginning of this module, you were introduced to the final project, **an Interactive Customizer**, where students apply their learning to design and code a dynamic, personalized web app.\r\n\r\n#### Now that you’ve explored the lessons and practiced the same coding tools and logic structures, you can see how each skill builds toward this culminating experience.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Support along the way\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/137da4d1ddb53c311d772c15affc3b5c-image-1762456148561.png\" alt=\"icons for bots that support along the way\" width=\"750px\" style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\r\n\r\n#### Students can choose which tool best supports their current task: brainstorming ideas, organizing their plan, or sketching out their logic and design.\r\n\r\n#### 🔁 **Circulate: As students explore the hub, ask guiding questions such as:**\r\n- #### “What type of interaction or outcome are you imagining for your app?”\r\n- ####“Which of these tools will help you move your idea forward right now?”\r\n- ####“How does your planned logic connect to the kind of experience you want your user to have?”\r\n\r\n#### Use these check-ins to confirm students are moving from idea to planning, rather than jumping straight into code.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #a6e3e8; border-radius: 40px; color: #000000; width: 95%; padding: 1px 20px 1px 20px;\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 16px; \"> <b> 💡Teaching Tip:</b> Set expectations for pacing — Milestone 1 can typically be finished by the end of today's class or early next class. Encourage students to focus first on clarity of idea rather than polish\r\n</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## You did it! \r\n\r\n#### You’ve now practiced using the tools to build this project while getting an overview of much of the Unit 2 content. This module is designed to give you a strong head start as you prepare to teach the unit.\r\n\r\n## Want to try more? \r\n\r\n#### If you’d like to try to complete the full project, open the link in a new tab and return to it after finishing this module.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;\">\r\n    ➡️ The project is in Lesson 11. You can find more details in the full <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-semester2-2025/units/2/lessons/11' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>lesson plan</a>.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n#### As you wrap up this module, take some time to reflect. Think about one of the following and share your feelings. \r\n\r\n>- ####How do you see students expressing their creativity through this project?\r\n>- #### How might using AI in this unit empower students as independent learners?\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display: flex; align-items: left; margin:20px 0px 30px 0px\">\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://forum.code.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/7dbe63a051fbad4ef262d6ab710e2966-image-1731959037460.png\" style=\"width: auto; height: 100px;\"  alt=\"A browser with two text boxes, both including an avatar and lines of text.\"></a>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #007786; border-radius: 20px 20px 20px 20px; color: #000000; width: 80%; margin-left: 5%; margin-right: 5%; padding: 10px 10px 5px 10px;\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"color: white; line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; font-size: 18px\"><b>Post to the Code.org Forum</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"color: white; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; font-size: 18px\">Share your response and read other educators' ideas on the forum! Click on the icon to the left to direct to our forum post.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n",
